# 11. RFC 6238 TOTP Authenticator

Audit the entire TOTP implementation and its integration with login entries.

Verify compatibility with RFC 6238 and the relevant HOTP algorithm requirements.

Inspect:

- Secret encoding and decoding.
- Base32 handling.
- HMAC algorithm.
- Time-step calculation.
- Unix time handling.
- Number of digits.
- Truncation.
- Leading zeros.
- Time synchronization assumptions.
- Countdown timer.
- UI refresh behavior.
- Secret storage.
- Invalid or malformed secrets.

Use published test vectors to verify the cryptographic output.

Do not rely solely on visually plausible six-digit values.

Test known test-vector inputs at known timestamps and verify exact expected results.

Confirm that the default six-digit, 30-second configuration works correctly and that any additional supported parameters are handled consistently.

For the animated countdown ring, verify that:

- The displayed remaining time is accurate.
- The countdown resets at the correct time boundary.
- The animation does not drift significantly.
- Backgrounding and foregrounding do not leave a stale code displayed as current.
- The UI refreshes when the app resumes.
- Timer callbacks do not leak after the screen is destroyed.
- Multiple instances do not create duplicate timers.
- Invalid secrets fail safely.
- Secrets remain concealed and encrypted.

Test behavior under delayed callbacks and device clock changes.

A TOTP code is time-sensitive. Do not continue presenting an expired code as valid simply because an animation has stalled.

